; descend_to_check FAILURE inside a 3-factor join. The bound $x resolves to a 2-byte
; symbol; at factor 3 the size byte (0xC2) EXISTS but the payload mismatches for the
; first sibling and matches for a LATER one. An over- or under-ascend after the failed
; check corrupts the caller's cursor and silently drops the later sibling.
(f aa)
(f bb)
(g aa)
(g bb)
(h aa)
(h ab)
(h ba)
(h bb)
(exec 0 (, (f $x) (g $x) (h $x)) (, (out $x)))
